        <p>WARRINGTON UNION.—The GUARDIANS are PREPARED TO RECEIVE TENDERS for the supply of 300 tons Granite Breakers to be delivered free at the Workhouse by cart, or by rail to the Work- house Siding (Cheshire Lines Railway). Sealed tenders endorsed "Tender for Granite Breakers," together with samples, must reach me not later than 10 a.m. on Thursday. the 25th inst. By Order. ' ARTHUR BOTTOMLEY, Clerk.</p>
        <p>Bewsey Chambers Warrington, 20th Mareb, 1909.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON UNION.—The GUARDIANS are PREPARED to RECTIIVE TENDERS for the supply of Macintosh Sheeting required at the Work- house during the Halt-year ending 2nd October 1909. Estimated quantity required 200 yards, width 36in. The sheeting to be supplied must be in accordance with sample to be obtained from the Master of the Workhouse. The price per yard including coat of delivery must be stated. Sealed tenders endorsed "Tender for Macintosh Sheeting" must reach me not later than 10 a.m on Friday, the 26th inst. By order, ARTHUR BOTTOMLEY, Clerk. Bewsey Chambers Warrington, 20th, March, 1909.</p>
