      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-03-20_WidnesExaminer_art0033" n="art0033">
        <p>cr</p>
        <p>Hockey</p>
        <p>Latchford visited Eccles last Saturday and the home team showed such poor form that 12 goals were regis- tered against them without the opposing goal being lowered. The game was of course very one-sided. Scott scored five goals, Banks and Parker three each,and Newell one.</p>
        <p>To-day the First Eleven are to play Preston at Latchford and their tearmis :—W. Unsworth, goal ; C Plinston, L. Kenworthy, halves : F. Newell, J. B Wilkinson, J. Albinson, balves ; D. Travis, H. Parker, H, Scott, E. Banks, W. Spensley, forwards. Referee : Mr. W. B. 'Cobb. Bully-off 2.30 prompt.</p>
        <p>The Second Eleven play their return game with Bury " A " at Bury and their team is :—W. H. Pickles, goal; J. Wilkinson, A. Allender, tacks; A. Newton, A. Knight, A. Knight, F. Tole, halves ; El. pooth, W. B. Smith, W. H. Minards. A. Starkey, C. Hackney, forwards. Referee :—Nfr. H. Warburton. Train from Central Station 1.50 p.m.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-03-20_WidnesExaminer_art0034" n="art0034">
        <head>NORTHERN UNION CUP.-SECOND ROUND.</head>
        <p>NORTHERN UNION CUP.-SECOND ROUND.</p>
