      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-03-20_WidnesExaminer_art0091" n="art0091">
        <head>GREEN OLD AGE.</head>
        <p>GREEN OLD AGE.</p>
        <p>TAKING ANOTHER LEASE OF LIFE THROI-GH THE MEDIUM OF A HEALTHY AND WELL-REGULATED SYSTEM, ASSISTED BY DR. MORSE'S INDIAN ROOT PILLS.</p>
        <p>To reach a green old age and enjoy good health can only be attained by the care of the system, which may at times require a little assistance. Tlr, first essential to good health is to keep the sto a sound condition. It is not the quantity .of food we cat, but what we digest .and assimilate that nourishes the body. Growing old ought not to mean growing weak and feeble. It 0.,-.) not mean weakness or feebleness foi- those who cat with a good appetite. and sound diges- % • tion. It is therefore of the utmost importance that old people .should retain the power to digest and assimi- late food which is the sole source of physical strength. When age brings feebleuess it is _generally because of</p>
        <p>the failure to assimilate</p>
        <p>nutrition contained in food.. To those in declining years who find that Nature responds less -readily to the demands made upon her, and- who need a mild, yet searching remedy, to keep their system in proper working order, there is nothing like Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills. _</p>
