vacity and att;'l,. tiveness. Mr. Hardy-Jackson -does excellently tf; not too easy part of Geoffery Challoner, and sir*, his sentimental songs with the true depth of fee'-' Mr. W. 0. Billington is most amusing as Sir Josl Verity, and other partS are .very capably played, Miss Florence Hylton, Miss Hilda Darrell, Mr. Burchill (as the Rajah of Bong) and Mr. IL 11. Bettram. The chorus is powerful and 'ceoir trained and plays a creditable part in the many _ _</p>
