        <p>A WEEK OF SHAKESPEARE. Next week a big attraction is announced for tbi; patrons of the Royal Court Theatre, when the f.'„te Benson North Shakespearean Comp Any pay a w 010'0 return visit. The company which consists of overkoo experienced artistes includes that popular Warrinetei favourite Mr. Henry Herbert. Since he last vis'te this town Mr. Herbert has added more to his reptied tion and both press and public are unanimously agreo that this clever young actor is one of the be exponents of Shakespeare in the Kingdom. He vvilsoo capably supported by Miss Gladys Vanderzee who a member of Mr. Beerbohm Tree's company and sylwoo an actress of high merit and exceptional brillilOto Over 20 tons of scenery are carried by the comparlll,4l largest amount ever staged in Warrington. 5p7.30 prices are quoted for schools and it is pleasing to 010 that sets are rapidly booking and all intending pat11:10 should secure their seats, as large houses will be,:a order of the week. All letters of enquiry regaro:be prices tr.c., should be sent to Mr. W. H. Sivery, director of the company, at the Theatre.</p>
        <p>Warrington Works Bowling Association. The annual meeting of the above was held at Bowling Green Inn on Thursday evening to he reports on last year's competition and disc 0: the prospects of the coming season. The seeret;l;) (Mr. W: Patrick) in his report said they had to of I very successful season in every way. The winner:oo the competition were Whitecross° No. 1 and it Ar the opinion of not a few that so long as the corproe tion was played at Bank Quay and under the 6440 f conditions, they had a chance second to none ig winning. Much had been done by the associatioo foster good feeling between man and and the future was full of hope and With regard to the financial side, the associO`iii, started with a deficit and finished with a balance. hand of £1 Bs. sd. £6O 9s. 2d. had been reee from various sources and the expenditure was Os. 9d. The above did not include the charity 1129:y the total receipts of which were £l6 15s. 10d.,and of expenditure -12 7s. 9d. leaving a balance in 1130-00 £l4 18s. ld, to be divided between the Infirmar the Nursing Association. The report was adoPne.lo Captain G. R. Crosfield was again elected pre'7,o4 of the association, Mr. Patrick was re-elected secr7l and Mr. \ Campbell, treasurer.—The following form the committee :—Messrs. J. Willett, W. Rail' if. F. Dean, H. Holborn, R. Savoury, G. Ball (jun.)' f• Horrabin, I. Makin, T. O'Brien, W. Simmister,,d Tynan.—Mr. Patrick ' was thanked - far his ,rao services, also Mr. Willett for acting as chairw during the evening.</p>
